# Tests skipped in VillageSQL CI, passed to mysql-test-run.pl via
# --skip-test-list from villagesql/bld_tools/test_ci.sh. This is in addition to
# tests disabled by the normal disabled.def files.
#
# Prefer not to add entries here. VillageSQL's convention, established by the
# 8.4.8 merge, is to skip at the feature level -- build_ci.sh turns the feature
# off and the suite notices and skips itself -- or to guard inside the test.
# This file is only for tests that neither mechanism reaches, and every entry
# should be a bug worth fixing rather than a permanent exclusion.
#
# Entry format is fixed by mysql-test/lib/mtr_cases.pm and validated on load, so
# a malformed line fails the whole run rather than being ignored:
#
#   <suite>.<test> [@platform|@!platform] : <BUG|WL>#<XXXX> [<comment>]
#
# The <BUG|WL>#<digits> token is mandatory and the trailing comment must be 79
# characters or fewer. That requirement is upstream Oracle's, unchanged since at
# least mysql-8.4.0 -- not something Percona or VillageSQL added -- so entries
# need a tracking number even when the cause is fully understood.
#
# BUG#0 means "no tracking issue filed yet". It satisfies the validator without
# pointing at someone else's bug database. Replace it with a real number when
# one exists; grep for BUG#0 to find entries still owed an issue.

percona.coredump : BUG#0 Placeholder id; no WITH_COREDUMPER=OFF guard, hangs to 900s timeout
